        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: حزب",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حزب — ḥizb — \"a political party\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لكل حزب برنامج مختلف. li-kulli ḥizb barnāmaj mukhtalif. Each party has a different programme."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: أحزاب, aḥzāb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حزب (ḥizb) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-z-b (Lane), where it names a band of people who hold together. Modern Arabic gave it the political party."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
