              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حملة — ḥamla — \"a campaign\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بدأت الحملة قبل شهرين. badaʾat al-ḥamla qabla shahrayn. The campaign began two months ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حملة (ḥamla) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-m-l, \"to carry, to bear\" (Lane). A ḥamla is one charge, one carrying forward: an attack, and so a campaign."
            }
          ]
        },
