              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ترشح — tarashshaḥa — \"to run for office\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ترشحت جارتنا في الانتخابات. tarashshaḥat jāratunā fī al-intikhābāt. Our neighbour ran in the elections."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يترشح, yatarashshaḥ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes لـ for the post one runs for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ترشح (tarashshaḥa) is built on the native Arabic root r-sh-ḥ, \"to sweat, to ooze\" (Lane). It is Form V, to make oneself ready for a post: to stand as a candidate."
